   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Water flows into and out of a tank. Let A(t) be the amount of water in the tank, in gallons, at time t hours, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). The rate of change of A is \\( R(t) = 4 t + 6 \\) gallons per hour. At time t = 1, there are 85 gallons. Find the value of \\( A(2) \\), in gallons, and show the setup for the calculation.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 97,
      "units": "gallons"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The known value and the accumulated change combine as \\( A(2) = A(1) + \\int_{1}^{2} \\left(4 t + 6\\right)\\,dt \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99033",
         "rule_named": "net change theorem"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the rate is \\( 2 t^{2} + 6 t \\), so the integral is \\( \\left[2 t^{2} + 6 t\\right]_{1}^{2} = 12 \\).",
         "mathjson": 12,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So \\( A(2) = 85 + 12 = 97 \\) gallons.",
         "mathjson": 97,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "combine with the known value"
      }
   ],
